            <title>1.2.12</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:11:58 -0500</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1.2.12</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.2.12</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### ⌘V pastes the thing you just made

Screenshots always went straight onto the clipboard. Recordings, trimmed
recordings, GIFs and marked-up pictures did not, so pressing ⌘V right after
one pasted whatever you had copied before it. Now everything Cubby makes is
on the clipboard the moment it is saved.

In a terminal, ⌘V pastes the file's path, ready for a CLI. Everywhere else
you get the picture, the animated GIF or the recording file, and never a
path in the middle of an email.

Pictures you edit in Preview from Cubby land on the clipboard too.
]]></description>
